 First, we break down the problem: we need to count the number of ways to form a 9-member tournament committee where one team (the host) selects 3 members out of 7, and each of the other 3 teams selects 2 members out of 7. The number of ways to choose 3 members from 7 is $\binom{7}{3}$, and the number of ways to choose 2 members from 7 is $\binom{7}{2}$. Since there are 4 teams, and each team hosts once, we need to consider the permutations of the host team among the 4 teams. The calculation is: \[
\text{Total ways} = 4 \times \binom{7}{3} \times \binom{7}{2} \times \binom{7}{2} \times \binom{7}{2}
