 Given the equation $|x + y - 7| + |4x - y + 12| = 0$, since both terms are absolute values, each must separately equal zero. This gives us the system of linear equations: \[
\begin{cases} x + y - 7 = 0 \\ 4x - y + 12 = 0 \end{cases}
\] Solving this system of equations will provide the values of $x$ and $y$. </think> <answer> $(1,-6)$ </answer>

